"week":1,"opp":"NO","qtr":3,"time":"05:13","down":1,"togo":7,"spot":"DET 7","text":"(5:13) (No Huddle) 5-K.Miller up the middle to DET 8 for -1 yards (46-J.Campbell).","epa":0.66,"wpa":0.007,"yards":-1,"score":"21-0","role":"tackle for loss"}],"zones":{"pass":{},"recv":{},"rush":{}},"splits":{},"reports":[{"week":9,"injury":"Neck","gameStatus":"Out","practice":"Did Not Participate In Practice"}],"weeklyStatus":[{"week":1,"status":"ACT","detail":"A01"},{"week":2,"status":"ACT","detail":"A01"},{"week":3,"status":"ACT","detail":"A01"},{"week":4,"status":"ACT","detail":"A01"},{"week":5,"status":"ACT","detail":"A01"},{"week":7,"status":"ACT","detail":"A01"},{"week":8,"status":"ACT","detail":"A01"},{"week":9,"status":"RES","detail":"R01"},{"week":10,"status":"RES","detail":"R01"},{"week":11,"status":"RES","detail":"R01"}],"espn":{"summaryLabel":"2026 regular season stats","summary":[{"name":"soloTackles","label":"SOLO","value":"29","rank":"Tied-94th"},{"name":"sacks","label":"Sacks","value":"0","rank":"Tied-360th"},{"name":"fumblesForced","label":"Forced Fumbles","value":"0","rank":"Tied-217th"},{"name":"interceptions","label":"Interceptions","value":"0","rank":"Tied-161st"}],"birthPlace":"Cedar Falls, IA","draftText":"2023: Rd 1, Pk 18 (DET)"},"news":[{"headline":"NFL Week 9 arrivals: Justin Jefferson rocks black leather trench coat before 'MNF'","description":"NFL stars continue to turn gameday arrivals into their own weekly fashion showcase.","published":"2026-11-10T01:12:56.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50393510/nfl-week-9-fashionable-arrivals","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN Staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lions' Jack Campbell has full movement in lower body after neck injury","description":"Lions All-Pro linebacker Jack Campbell released a statement Wednesday saying he has full movement in his lower body and is making progress with movement in his upper body as he recovers from a neck injury, suffered in Sunday's game.","published":"2026-11-04T21:37:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50380067/lions-lb-campbell-full-movement-lower-body-neck-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lions LB Jack Campbell still in hospital, but signs positive","description":"Lions linebacker Jack Campbell is still in the hospital for evaluation and monitoring of a neck injury, but the team said in a statement \"preliminary indications are positive.\"","published":"2026-11-02T20:29:55.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50360680/lions-lb-jack-campbell-hospital-signs-positive","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lions linebacker Jack Campbell placed on backboard, carted off vs. Vikings","description":"Lions All-Pro linebacker Jack Campbell was placed on a backboard and carted off the field early in the fourth quarter Sunday against the Vikings.","published":"2026-11-02T00:32:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50350934/lions-linebacker-jack-campbell-placed-backboard-carted-off","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Emotional All-Pro LB Campbell shoulders blame for Lions' loss","description":"Jack Campbell fought back tears while reflecting on Detroit's poor defensive effort in Thursday night's loss in Buffalo.","published":"2026-09-18T12:50:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/49970421/emotional-all-pro-lb-campbell-shoulders-blame-lions-loss","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Why Lions, NFL coaches believe Super Bowl chances are real","description":"If you don't believe Campbell & Co. that the Lions will be contenders, ask Sean McVay, Matt LaFleur and others.","published":"2026-08-21T15:51:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/49651690/detroit-lions-super-bowl-window-opportunity-2026","type":"Story","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 Detroit Lions training camp: Latest intel, updates","description":"Catch up on our daily updates from Lions training camp, including intel on QBs, position battles and potential breakouts.","published":"2026-08-13T20:28:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/49419620/detroit-lions-training-camp-2026-intel-updates","type":"Story","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"LB Jack Campbell: I wanted to be a Lion, no matter what","description":"Jack Campbell plans to stay laser focused this offseason as a core member of the group trying to help Detroit bounce back from a disappointing 9-8 season.","published":"2026-05-27T23:21:24.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/48893737/lb-jack-campbell-wanted-lion-no-matter-what","type":"Story","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Jack Campbell, Lions reach 4-year, $81M extension","description":"The Lions have signed Jack Campbell to a four-year extension, putting him under contract with the franchise through the 2030 season. The deal is for $81 million and includes $51.5M guaranteed, sources told NFL Network's Ian Rapoport.","published":"2026-05-21T23:36:46.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/48836875/lions-sign-all-pro-lb-jack-campbell-four-year-extension","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Source: Lions pick up Gibbs' 5th-year option, decline Campbell's","description":"The Lions have picked up the fifth-year option on running back Jahmyr Gibbs' contract but declined the option on Jack Campbell's deal, a source confirmed to ESPN.","published":"2026-04-28T23:57:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/48621631/source-lions-pick-gibbs-5th-year-option-decline-campbells","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Jack Campbell (American football)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jack_Campbell_(American_football)","description":"American football player (born 2000)","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:16Z","intro":"Jack Campbell (born August 22, 2000) is an American professional football linebacker for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He was a unanimous All-American playing college football for the Iowa Hawkeyes, winning the Butkus Award in 2022. Campbell was selected by the Lions in the first round of the 2023 NFL draft, and named to the All-Rookie Team. He earned his first Pro Bowl and All-Pro selections in 2025, as well as being the professional Butkus Award recipient.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Campbell attended Cedar Falls High School in Cedar Falls, Iowa. As a Junior and Senior, he led Cedar Falls to back-to-back 4A State Basketball Championships in 2018 and 2019, respectively. During his football career he had a school record 338 career tackles. He committed to the University of Iowa to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman at Iowa in 2019, Campbell played in 11 games and had five tackles. As a sophomore in 2020, he played in five games and had 29 tackles, one sack and one interception. He returned as a starter his junior year in 2021, recording 140 tackles, two interceptions, a sack and a touchdown. After the 2021 season, Campbell was named first-team all Big Ten, leading one of the best defenses in the country.\nCampbell returned to Iowa in 2022 and was named the preseason Big Ten defensive player of the year by Big Ten media. Campbell led the elite Iowa defense in 2022 to a nationwide best in yards per play average and top five in total defense and defensive efficiency. Campbell finished the regular season with 118 tackles, ranking second in the Big Ten and tied for 13th nationally, adding two interceptions, one recovered fumble and one forced fumble. Against Minnesota, Campbell's forced fumble and long interception return, both in the fourth quarter, enabled Iowa's victory despite being outgained and having much less time of possession.\nFollowing the season, Campbell was given the 2022 Butkus Award as the top linebacker in college football as well as the William V. Campbell Trophy as a scholar-athlete. He was also named the Big Ten's Nagurski–Woodson Defensive Player of the Year and Butkus–Fitzgerald Linebacker of the Year."},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"Campbell was selected with the 18th pick in the 2023 NFL draft by the Detroit Lions. Campbell recorded his first career sack in a Week 3, 20–6 victory over the Atlanta Falcons. Following the end of the regular season, Campbell was named to the PFWA All-Rookie Team.\nOn April 28, 2026, the Lions declined the fifth-year option on Campbell's contract, making him set to become a free agent after the 2026 season. However, on May 21, the Lions signed Campbell to a four-year, $81 million contract extension that runs through the 2030 season.\nOn November 1, 2026, during a Week 8 matchup against the Minnesota Vikings, Campbell was involved in a tackle on Vikings tight end T. J. Hockenson in which he suffered a neck injury that left him lying on the field motionless for more than eight minutes. He was transported to a local hospital where he underwent evaluation overnight and treatment. On November 4, Campbell released a statement revealing he had full movement in his lower extremities, and he was still making progress with movement in his upper extremities. He was placed on injured reserve on November 7."},{"key":"personal","title":"Personal life","text":"Campbell is a Christian. He is married to Megan Campbell. They have one son together."}],"wikidataId":"Q110442823","social":{}},"transactions":[{"date":"2026-11-07","text":"Placed LB Jack Campbell on injured reserve. Signed DB Nick Whiteside to the active roster. Elevated DE Anthony Lucas and RB Jabari Small from the practice squad."},{"date":"2026-05-21","text":"Signed LB Jack Campbell to a four-year contract extension."}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4569465","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/C/CampJa04.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/jack-campbell/101515","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/jack-campbell/10842","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jack_Campbell_(American_football)"},"insights":["Ranks 5th of 79 qualified linebackers in missed-tackle %.","On the field for 68% of Detroit’s defensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $4.8M is the 14th-largest on the roster.","Under contract through 2030.","Drafted 18th overall in 2023 (round 1) by DET."]}